# The formal gate has to be enforced by the GRAMMAR, not only by the lexer.
#
# `|->', `|=>', `disable iff' and `endproperty' are tokens the lexer only
# produces in formal mode, so every production that needs one is already gated.
# An inline property spec that starts with a clocking event is spelled entirely
# with tokens that have always existed, so it is reachable without `-formal' and
# must refuse itself. Without this, a plain synthesis read would silently accept
# an assertion and emit a $check cell where it used to hard-error.
logger -expect error "only accepted with .read_verilog -formal" 1
read_verilog -sv <<EOT
module top (input clk, input a, input b);
	assert property (@(posedge clk) !(a && b));
endmodule
EOT
